WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.959 --> 00:00:07.720
I am actually a student in international economic relations.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.800
I am 23 years old and I come from Poland.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.159
I'm 74, I am a former teacher

00:00:17.159 --> 00:00:18.519
and I come from Belgium.

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:22.720
I am a telecommunications retiree

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.879
I am 77 years old and I come from Cyprus

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.519
I am 19 years old and I live in Spain.

00:00:34.639 --> 00:00:36.720
where I study at University.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.360
We are four citizens from different nationalities

00:00:45.039 --> 00:00:48.920
and we are here on a special mission.

00:01:17.039 --> 00:01:19.560
This has been an intense experience

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.680
in the power of participatory democracy,

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.119
after months of discussions and powerful debates.

00:01:27.039 --> 00:01:29.000
Today is Europe Day.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.639
It marks the end of our work as citizens

00:01:32.639 --> 00:01:36.239
on the Conference on the Future of Europe.

00:01:36.239 --> 00:01:39.759
It's the moment where we deliver our conclusions

00:01:39.759 --> 00:01:41.639
to the European institutions.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:47.159
It's a very important event.

00:01:47.159 --> 00:01:50.479
It's a huge democratic experiment.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.119
This is a new process.

00:01:54.119 --> 00:01:59.800
We are the first people to do it,
so it has been very difficult.

00:02:01.519 --> 00:02:02.920
There is a lot of emotion,

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.479
because it is the result of many weeks' work.

00:02:07.479 --> 00:02:11.119
We can't say it's over, but it is a big step.

00:02:21.159 --> 00:02:24.800
Citizens from all 27 member states were randomly selected.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.200
800 citizens in total.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.119
It's an innovation, because besides these citizen panels,

00:02:30.119 --> 00:02:33.400
there is a digital platform. So everyone can participate.

00:02:35.159 --> 00:02:37.879
Their aim is to have a broad reflection

00:02:37.879 --> 00:02:39.400
about the future of the European Union,

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.920
be it economic, political, social.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:45.879
Then these ideas will be fine-tuned,

00:02:45.879 --> 00:02:48.400
in order to then become
recommendations for politicians:

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.400
MPs, national ministers and so on.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:06.159
When travelling through Europe I feel more European.

00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:12.039
I like travelling a lot because I discover new cultures,

00:03:12.039 --> 00:03:16.720
new ways of seeing the world.
Also, the people are very interesting.

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:30.159
I was selected in a totally random way.

00:03:30.159 --> 00:03:33.639
I was very happy. I then explained it to my parents

00:03:33.639 --> 00:03:36.800
and they told me it was probably a scam.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:42.720
So, I wasn't really sure about coming,

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.360
but in the end, I came and I'm glad I did.

00:03:48.639 --> 00:03:51.000
It was was very impressive,

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:56.319
arriving from a small country like Belgium

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:58.319
and meeting people from all the other European countries.

00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:03.280
So, very quickly the Belgian dimension became a European dimension.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:08.439
Of course I knew that I would keep my DNA and my Belgian identity,

00:04:08.439 --> 00:04:11.959
but I instantly felt part of the group with all the others.

00:04:15.159 --> 00:04:18.000
I had a proposal to join the working group

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.239
of economy, social justice and jobs.

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:22.319
And I thought: it's a brilliant opportunity

00:04:22.319 --> 00:04:26.519
because I could tell them about young people's perspectives

00:04:26.519 --> 00:04:31.079
and our economic position in the world.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.759
This is for the translation, okay?

00:04:34.759 --> 00:04:35.879
Thank you very much.

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:44.239
At the beginning, I made some proposals.

00:04:44.239 --> 00:04:46.720
To improve democracy.

00:04:55.479 --> 00:04:59.879
My dream for Europe concerns our children and grandchildren,

00:04:59.879 --> 00:05:04.000
the young people of Europe.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.720
I believe they will have a better future,

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:11.280
without employment-related problems,

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:16.920
without war and conflict between countries

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:21.280
This is what we expect from the EU.

00:05:28.039 --> 00:05:33.600
I focused on anti-discrimination and security.

00:05:34.039 --> 00:05:38.639
For me, the question of quality of life was important.

00:05:38.639 --> 00:05:41.000
Our life should not depend only on work

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:45.639
it should rather be a good balance
between personal life and work.

00:05:47.159 --> 00:05:51.800
In the first session, the citizens bring up fairly general things.

00:05:52.519 --> 00:05:56.519
In the second session, they re-examine these main ideas and refine them

00:05:58.159 --> 00:06:02.119
The third session consists of drafting orientations,

00:06:02.119 --> 00:06:04.079
making recommendations that are much more concrete

00:06:04.079 --> 00:06:07.280
and more likely to speak to decision-makers.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:14.280
Because we are so different,

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:18.879
there were times when it was
very difficult for us to agree

00:06:18.879 --> 00:06:21.800
and keep everybody happy.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:26.839
But I think we've done an amazing job in our group.

00:06:27.239 --> 00:06:29.680
What we are going to do this weekend:

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.280
We will have five orientations from our group.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:38.039
The job of a facilitator as a neutral person

00:06:38.039 --> 00:06:42.600
is to bring the citizens through this process.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:45.360
To ensure that they are in this process

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:49.759
where they start from a very broad vision for the EU

00:06:49.759 --> 00:06:51.519
to the specific recommendations.

00:06:51.519 --> 00:06:53.800
It works with the help of the translators

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:56.119
who are remote, working online.

00:06:56.119 --> 00:07:00.079
There's actually a pretty immediate translation, at most a few seconds' delay.

00:07:00.079 --> 00:07:04.360
The floor is now to Mr. Kacper Parol, who is the spokesperson

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:07.239
of the citizens in the working group 'Economy'.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:12.280
We had a lot of feedback for our proposals.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:17.119
Some of the politicians didn't really agree

00:07:17.119 --> 00:07:21.879
with some of the issues citizens mentioned.

00:07:21.879 --> 00:07:25.519
Because they are learning too, about the Conference and the process.

00:07:25.519 --> 00:07:29.479
So once they learned about the process, they were more appreciative.

00:07:29.479 --> 00:07:34.519
Our panel 4 recommends a complete review of all agreements

00:07:34.519 --> 00:07:39.079
and laws related to asylum and migration in Europe.

00:07:39.079 --> 00:07:43.680
We've only got three years left
to reverse the greenhouse gas emissions trend,

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.639
not forgetting the water shortages ahead of us.

00:07:47.519 --> 00:07:49.360
Climate action is now or never.

00:07:49.639 --> 00:07:52.560
At the beginning, it was a little difficult
with the politicians,

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:56.800
who directed us like one directs
a meeting when one is in politics.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:00.079
So we had fewer opportunities
to talk to each other.

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:03.119
So there, we had to reverse the trend a bit.

00:08:03.119 --> 00:08:05.079
And it happened gradually,

00:08:05.079 --> 00:08:09.360
and the end result is really what we expected:

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:12.439
to be able to speak out, to be listened to.

00:08:16.519 --> 00:08:21.680
Our goal is for our voice, the voice of European citizens,
to be heard in the European Union.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:27.039
This is what we will be asking for 
from the competent European Union bodies tomorrow.

00:08:37.839 --> 00:08:40.560
I think we now know that this sort of experience

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:44.759
of involving ordinary citizens in big debates about policy, it works!

00:08:44.759 --> 00:08:48.479
And now we're seeing, in a multilingual environment

00:08:48.479 --> 00:08:50.479
with simultaneous translation,

00:08:50.479 --> 00:08:53.600
citizens from 27 member states of the European Union

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:55.839
discussing really complex issues

00:08:55.839 --> 00:08:58.560
and coming forward with very important proposals.

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:01.119
So it's a good process, it should be used.

00:09:02.319 --> 00:09:06.759
You have proven that this form of democracy works.

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:10.879
And I believe we should give it more room.

00:09:10.879 --> 00:09:14.159
It should become part of the way we make policy.

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.239
So there's no time to waste.

00:09:18.159 --> 00:09:21.200
Let's be loyal to the outcome of the conference.

00:09:21.879 --> 00:09:24.879
Let's implement its conclusions as soon as possible,

00:09:24.879 --> 00:09:27.039
because it's the will of the people

00:09:27.039 --> 00:09:29.680
and let the will of the people prevail.

00:09:37.159 --> 00:09:39.759
I feel that citizens should be more involved

00:09:39.759 --> 00:09:42.680
in the day-to-day European Union work.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:47.360
But I think that the Conference is also a great lesson

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:49.639
for our national governments.

00:09:51.639 --> 00:09:55.800
We are very proud because all our efforts,

00:09:55.800 --> 00:10:01.159
those of us who have been in the working groups,

00:10:01.159 --> 00:10:07.680
are coming to an end and will now start to take shape

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:12.600
as they enter the phase of realisation.

00:10:14.759 --> 00:10:17.920
For me, it was an extraordinary experience

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:21.560
because being called, at the age of seventy-four,

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:23.159
to talk about the future of Europe...

00:10:23.159 --> 00:10:27.000
It was probably not for me that I came here,

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.639
but for my grandchildren.

00:10:31.439 --> 00:10:36.759
I'm taking back with me the hope that Europe will be something...

00:10:36.759 --> 00:10:42.439
That it will be a little more
what I want in the future when I am older.

00:10:42.439 --> 00:10:48.280
I hope to be able to live in the Europe
we have imagined here.

00:10:52.039 --> 00:10:54.439
The Conference on the future of Europe delivered 49 proposals

00:10:54.439 --> 00:10:57.759
with more than 300 measures to improve the EU.

00:10:57.759 --> 00:11:02.759
It is Europe's biggest ever experiment
in participatory democracy.

00:11:02.759 --> 00:11:06.039
The members of the European Parliament are committed to ensuring

00:11:06.039 --> 00:11:10.600
the Conference's vision of the EU of tomorrow becomes reality.

